within MicroPythonMCU.Interfaces;

connector RadioAirInput "Causal logical input of the micro:bit radio air link (board side) - mirror image of RadioAirOutput"
  input Integer networkId "Id of the radio network: all the antennas wired to the same Peripherals.Radio.RadioAir hear each other, see its documentation";
  annotation(
    Icon(coordinateSystem(preserveAspectRatio = true, extent = {{-100, -100}, {100, 100}}), graphics = {Polygon(points = {{-100, 50}, {0, 0}, {-100, -50}, {-100, 50}}, lineColor = {160, 90, 0}, fillColor = {160, 90, 0}, fillPattern = FillPattern.Solid)}),
    Documentation(info = "<html>
<p>Causal connector (input) of the logical radio air link, on the <code>Antenna</code> port of <code>MicroBit_v2</code>: wire it with <code>connect()</code> to a <code>RadioAirOutput</code> (the <code>antenna</code> port of a <code>Peripherals.Radio.RadioAir</code>). No default value on the field (an unconditional default would conflict with the equation generated by <code>connect()</code>, cf. <code>DisplayLinkInput</code>): a board that uses <code>microbit.radio</code> must have its antenna wired. See <code>RadioAir</code> and the decision \"Radios micro:bit\" in <code>requirements.md</code>.</p>
</html>"));
end RadioAirInput;
